# Hero render for the README: 7JZU with the MolecularNodes-style look from
# chimenodes (https://github.com/anirudhbhashyam/chimenodes).
#
#   cd <repo root>
#   open -W -a /Applications/ChimeraX-<ver>.app --args \
#     --cmd "cd $PWD" --script "$PWD/docs/render_chimenodes.cxc"
#
# Both the --cmd and the absolute --script are load-bearing. `open` does not
# pass the shell's working directory to the app, so without `--cmd "cd $PWD"`
# the relative paths below fail with "No such file/path: tests/data/...", and
# a relative --script fails before the script is even read.
#
# Two things make this NOT runnable in CI, which is why render_structure.py stays:
#   - chimenodes needs an OpenGL 3.3 core context, and ChimeraX --offscreen on
#     macOS does not provide one ("could not enable rendering pipeline"), so it
#     has to go through the GUI app via `open -W`.
#   - it needs ChimeraX and the chimenodes bundle installed locally.
#
# The preset owns the background, so `set bgColor` has no effect here. The saved
# PNG is genuinely transparent (alpha 0 over ~89% of it); the warm tint you see
# in a viewer is the RGB under those transparent pixels. make_schematic.py
# composites it onto white.
open tests/data/7JZU_LCB1_RBD.pdb
hide atoms
show cartoon
color /B #c2c8cd
color /A #2f7fc0
chimenodes preset mn_default
view
turn y -25
turn x 10
turn z -62
zoom 0.88
save docs/structure_chimenodes.png width 2400 height 1500 supersample 3 transparentBackground true
exit
